%N A402183 Number of nonempty subsets of {1..n} whose sum divides their least common multiple.
%C A402183 Every singleton is counted, since its sum equals its least common multiple.
%e A402183 a(4) = 5: the subsets are {1}, {2}, {3}, {4} and {1,2,3}, the last having sum 6 and least common multiple 6.
%o A402183 (PARI) a(n) = my(s=0); forsubset(n, x, x=Vec(x); if(#x && lcm(x)%vecsum(x)==0, s++)); s; \\ _Andrew Howroyd_, Nov 14 2026
%Y A402183 Cf. A270970 (sum equals least common multiple), A326156 (sum divides product).
%K A402183 nonn,new
%O A402183 1,2
%A A402183 _Thibaut Forest_, Nov 14 2026
